        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 529990,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Morning all. Now that the SOP is firm, let's plan the training. I've created a draft Training Deck (A5) and a one-page Quick-Check for HCAs (A4). I've also proposed a training schedule for the pilot unit. Please review and share your thoughts. This is for T4 and T5.",
            "mentions": [
              5821,
              35334,
              382216,
              455653,
              523757
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "A5",
              "T4",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 382216,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "Thanks @529990, this is a great start. The checklist A4 is very clear and practical. For the training sessions, given the staffing constraints, a mix of short, live sessions plus the deck (A5) for async review seems like the best approach. What do you all think? D5",
            "mentions": [
              529990
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 455653,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "I agree with the mixed approach. The checklist A4 is perfect. I'd just suggest we print it on laminated cardstock so it lasts longer at the workstations. The proposed schedule in T5 looks reasonable, it covers both day and night shifts.",
